{{also|FET|Fet|fèt}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fɛt/|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|en|ped}}
From {{der|en|enm|fetten}}, {{m|enm|feten}}, from {{der|en|ang|fetian}}, {{m|ang|fatian||to bring, fetch}}, probably a conflation of {{der|en|gem-pro|*fetaną||to go}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ped-||to walk, stumble, fall}}; and {{der|en|gem-pro|*fatōną||to hold, seize}}, also from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ped-}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vatten||to catch, grab}}, {{cog|de|fassen||to lay hold of, seize, take, hold}}. Compare also {{cog|is|feta||to find one's way}}. More at {{m|en|fetch}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|fets|fetting|fet}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[fetch]].

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{m|en|feat}}, {{cog|fr|fait}}, and {{cog|it|fetta||slice}}, {{cog|de|Fetzen||rag}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[piece]].
#* Michael Drayton
#*: The bottom clear,<br>Now laid with many a '''fet'''<br>Of seed pearl.

===Etymology 3===

